NNAAMMEE
     bbhhnndd — Broadcom Home Networking Division interconnect bus

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     To compile this driver into the kernel, add the following lines to the
     kernel configuration file:

           ddeevviiccee bbhhnndd

     To load the driver as a module at boot, add this line to loader.conf(5):

           bhnd_load="YES"

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The bbhhnndd driver provides a unified kernel bus interface to the on-chip
     interconnects used in Broadcom Home Networking Division (HND) devices.

     The Broadcom HND device family consists of SoCs (System On a Chip) and
     host-connected chipsets based on a common library of Broadcom IP cores
     connected via an internal hardware bus architecture.  Drivers for these
     cores are implemented against the unified bbhhnndd interface.

     The Sonic Inc. Silicon Backplane used in earlier HND devices is supported
     by the siba(4) BHND driver.

     The ARM AMBA-based interconnect used in later HND devices is supported by
     the bcma(4) BHND driver.

